{"abstract":[{"text":"Tries over sequences of any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sets-of-sequences","title":"Sets of sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"]},{"anchor":"Dictionaries-keyed-by-sequences","title":"Dictionaries keyed by sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"]},{"anchor":"Pattern-matching","title":"Pattern matching","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton"]},{"anchor":"Extended-Modules","title":"Extended Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees"],"generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie"},{"type":"text","text":" is a set of sequences and a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" a dictionary keyed by them, both kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a trie (Fredkin, 1960): a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex paths spell the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keys. They answer the queries a hash set cannot: every key with a prefix"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements(withPrefix:)"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" is O(1)), whether any key has one ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPrefix(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the longest key that is a prefix of a query ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"longestPrefix(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Tries","","let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys are any sequence of the symbol type and are stored as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Symbol]"},{"type":"text","text":". For text, the symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type decides what a step is: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Character>"},{"type":"text","text":" steps by grapheme cluster, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by scalar, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<UInt8>"},{"type":"text","text":" over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"utf8"},{"type":"text","text":" by byte, the fastest of the three, because comparing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes is cheaper than comparing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Character"},{"type":"text","text":"s. When the symbols are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":", each vertex keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its children sorted, so iteration is in lexicographic order; otherwise children come in the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were added."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"},{"type":"text","text":" and a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" hold the same keys and answer the same queries,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the same names, in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): every chain of vertices with one child and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols, so there is a vertex per key and per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"branching point rather than per symbol. They suit keys with long shared prefixes, such as file"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paths or URLs, and build faster and in less memory than a trie of the same keys."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A trie’s shape converts to Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree(_:)"},{"text":", and a radix tree’s to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"text":" of its vertices’ prefixes with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence(_:)"},{"text":" (import Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trees"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module beside this one).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","type":"reference"},{"text":" (Aho and Corasick, 1975) finds every occurrence of any of a set of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patterns in one pass over a text, in O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"z","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") for ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" symbols and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"z"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" matches: a trie of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patterns with failure links. Its ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","type":"reference"},{"text":" is the automaton as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\").map(\\.patternIndex)   \/\/ [1, 0, 3]"],"type":"codeListing"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"Tries","externalID":"Tries","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"Tries"}]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tries"]}],"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTreeDictionary":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtreedictionary","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTreeDictionary"}],"title":"RadixTreeDictionary","abstract":[{"text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"chain of vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols, each key’s vertex holding its value.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTreeDictionary"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/tries","title":"Tries","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Tries over sequences of any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trie":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trie","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Trie","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A set of sequences kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paths spell the keys (Fredkin, 1960)."}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/StatesView-swift.struct/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","title":"symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The symbol a goto edge reads, or nil for a failure edge."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"ofEdgeAt"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.struct\/symbol(ofedgeat:)"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An automaton that finds every occurrence of every pattern of a set in one pass over a text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Aho and Corasick, 1975)."}],"fragments":